  "error": null,
  "output_text": "Keywords:  \n- Hematopoietic stem cell (HSC) program  \n- Granulocyte–monocyte progenitor (GMP) transition  \n- Neutrophil differentiation trajectory  \n- IL-1β → G-CSF inflammatory axis  \n\nCandidate Genes:  \n- Cebpa (key for GMP→granulocyte lineage commitment)  \n- Gfi1 (granulopoiesis regulator)  \n- Stat3 (downstream of G-CSF receptor signaling)  \n- Csf3 (G-CSF ligand)  \n- Il1b (TAM-derived IL-1β inducer)  \n\nRationale: Cebpa and Stat3 appear in the cluster membership (Cebpa in Down Late, Stat3 in Up Early), and all five genes are mechanistically tied to neutrophil‐specific developmental stages and the IL-1β/G-CSF cascade driving tumor-induced expansion.",
